Z||000003||Haze_Performance||09-14-2001||10:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>What brand is the bra that fits the '87 SE?  I didn't know there was an '88 SE.  Only a coupe, Formula and GT.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Heres a little bra info..<P>84 Indy, 86-87 SE, 85-88 GT: All the same<P>All coupes & 84 SE, 85 SE Along with Formulas are the same. <P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">                <BR></A><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole_6.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Monkeyman||09-15-2001||04:51 AM||||Haze--Wouldn't the Formula use the same bra as the '87/'88 coupes?  Would a bra that fits the earlier coupes also fit the later style fascias?<P>I think the brand I'm looking for is LaBra.  It basically covers the entire front fascia but not the hood.  A bra isn't my 1st priority right now, but I'd buy one if it was cheap enough.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||09-15-2001||11:01 AM||||Formula's cannot use the same as 84-85 SE's, but will use the 87-88 coupe bra.<P>All 84-86 coupes and 84-85 SE's use the same.<P>If the bra is for a Firebird it will not work on a Fiero... but you may want to at least fit it to yoiur Fiero to be sure its just not mis-labeled.<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2m6siga.JPG">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000006||cadaver||09-15-2001||01:14 PM||||And to answer the mans question No it wont fit.||||reg||1
